<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Margaret of Passavant</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1315</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Margaret of Passavant was a noblewoman of the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> and heiress of the Neuilly barons of Passavant. In the 1270s she claimed the barony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akova">Akova</a> through her mother's family, and the lawsuit before the prince's court, recorded in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chronicle-of-the-morea">Chronicle of the Morea</a>, became a famous case of Frankish feudal law. She recovered only part of the lands.</p></div>
